From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:12:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] browse: panorama comfortable grids flow as staggered grids
 with wider auto columns

The source browse page and the related-manga grid had the same two problems
as the library "Panorama comfortable grid" (previous commit):

- Auto columns used GridCells.Adaptive(128.dp), so a 3:2 cover was as wide as
  a book cover and only about two thirds as tall. Panorama mode now uses a
  168 dp minimum when the column count is auto. A fixed count stays fixed.
- LazyVerticalGrid makes every row as tall as its tallest cell, so a 2:3 cover
  beside a 3:2 cover left a hole under the wide one. Panorama mode now uses
  LazyVerticalStaggeredGrid (with the staggered fast scroller added for the
  library). Section headers and paging placeholders span the full line.

GridCells.Fixed.count is not readable, so the column preference is carried on
a GridCells that still lays out like Adaptive(128.dp) / Fixed for every
non-panorama mode. Season selection still builds a plain GridCells; that grid
falls back to the same library column preference.

Cover orientation is cached per manga (shared with the library) so a cell
keeps its shape when it scrolls back into view. In panorama mode an unknown
cover is assumed 16:9.

Harmony-only (follow-up to 0020): Mihon has no panorama cover feature, Animeko has no such grid.
